<ArticleLayout slug="amazon-product-image-requirements" ctaLabel="Create your account" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">Pure white, 85 percent of the frame, 1,000 pixels for zoom. Those three come straight from Amazon. Two things rarely reach the size guides: the places where Amazon's own pages disagree, and a new line saying Amazon may edit the files you send.</p>

  <h2>What are Amazon's product image requirements in 2026?</h2>

  <p>Amazon's product image requirements in 2026 center on the main image: pure white (RGB 255, 255, 255), with the product filling 85 percent of the frame, shown whole and only once. Files run 500 to 10,000 pixels on the longest side, 1,000 or more for zoom. hubStudio can build the files; Seller Central takes the upload.</p>

  <p>Reviewed October 17, 2026. Every rule below is quoted from Amazon's Seller Central help for the US store, read that day in a logged-out browser. The help pages carry no dates, so each row is dated by the read. Where two Amazon pages disagree, both values are printed and each page is named.</p>

