  <blockquote class="evidence">Amazon's main image must have "a pure white background (RGB color values: 255, 255, 255)" and should "Show the product as 85% of the image," whole, once and as one unit. Read from Amazon's own help article.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Amazon Seller Central, Product image guide, US store, page undated, read October 17, 2026. https://sellercentral.amazon.com/help/hub/reference/external/G1881</p>

  <p>How is the 85 percent measured? The guide doesn't say. Two other Amazon pages come close. The clothing page counts "85% of the total image area," for clothing. The error codes page gives an example instead: a product filling only 100 by 100 pixels of a 500 by 500 image is too small, because "at least 85% of a product image should be taken up with the product itself." For everything else the method stays open. Pick one and hold it across the catalog.</p>

  <p>Lifestyle main images exist, but barely. Amazon's style guide page names six product types that may use one: BED, BED_FRAME, MATTRESS, RUG, RUG_PAD and SOFA. Everything else goes on white.</p>

