  <p>Products removed from search show on the Fix tab in Manage Products. Files that failed show under Submission status, report type Content compliance issues. Then allow up to 24 hours for a replacement main image to appear.</p>

  <p>Not every failure waits for review. Some happen at upload. Amazon's upload errors page names two worth knowing before a reshoot. Error 990003 means the new main image shows a different product from the one on the ASIN. "Resubmission of previously accepted or rejected images" means the same file went in twice: change it (crop, resolution, a fresh export) and Amazon reads it as new.</p>

  <p>One sentence on the Product image guide is new this autumn. It wasn't there when we read the page on September 14.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">"We may also modify images that you submit to meet the product image requirements or enhance the customer experience." The sentence appears on the October 17 read, in English and in the page's Chinese version, and not on the September 14 read of the same address.</blockquote>
