  <p>The suppression page gives the example: Amazon may remove a watermark itself. Don't count on it. The same page lists a watermark on the main image as a reason to suppress the listing.</p>

  <h2>How do you make Amazon-ready product images in hubStudio?</h2>

  <p>Start from a photo of the real product. Amazon asks for real scale, quantity and color, so the honest route is to edit your own picture, not to invent the product from a prompt.</p>

  <p>In the <a href="/help/create-an-image">Image studio</a>, Edit an image takes your photo and an instruction, such as a pure white background or a stray object removed. Add the <a href="/help/skills">E-commerce packshot skill</a> from the Catalog, and Improve with AI rewrites your prompt with it. On the ChatGPT Image engines, pick an Opaque background and a resolution up to 4K (3840 pixels), which clears Amazon's 1,000-pixel zoom line with room to crop. Transparent, which only the 2.5 engines offer, is no use for a main image: it has to be white.</p>

  <p>Then open the result in the <a href="/help/assets-library#the-image-editor">Image editor</a>, which is free. Crop to Square 1:1 or draw your own frame, leaving about 85 percent fill. Save as JPG or PNG at the size you choose. Skip WebP here: it isn't on Amazon's list. The editor works on pictures up to 4,096 pixels on the long side.</p>

  <p>The upload is yours. hubStudio doesn't connect to Seller Central; files go in through <a href="https://sellercentral.amazon.com/help/hub/reference/external/GUGPCYWV2P8KVFUT">Upload images</a> or Image Manager.</p>

  <p>The <a href="/resources/how-to/ai-white-background-packshot">AI white-background packshot how-to</a> walks through the main image step by step, and the <a href="/resources/how-to/product-photo-to-lifestyle-image">product photo to lifestyle image how-to</a> covers the PT slots. Selling on Tmall and JD as well? The <a href="/resources/insights/amazon-tmall-jd-one-product-three-listings">one product, three listings piece</a> shows which Amazon files carry over. For the full listing built by a team, see the <a href="/services/design/ecommerce">ecommerce design service</a> and the <a href="/solutions/platforms/amazon">Amazon platform page</a>; the <a href="/resources/specs">platform specs library</a> holds the other networks.</p>

