  <h2>FAQ</h2>

  <h3>What are Amazon's main image requirements?</h3>

  <p>A pure white background, RGB 255, 255, 255. The product fills 85 percent of the frame and appears in full, a single unit shown once, with only the accessories that ship with it. No text, logos, watermarks, props, mannequins or placeholders. Packaging only when it's a real feature, multipacks aside. Adult clothing goes on a standing model; shoes go single, facing left, at 45 degrees.</p>

  <h3>What size should Amazon product images be?</h3>

  <p>Between 500 and 10,000 pixels on the longest side, and 1,000 or more if you want zoom, which Amazon recommends. Amazon sets no aspect ratio in its <a href="https://sellercentral.amazon.com/help/hub/reference/external/G1881">Product image guide</a>, though its clothing page asks for close to 3:4 on a clothing main image. One Amazon page says 500 on the shortest side, so keep both sides at 500 or more.</p>

  <h3>Does the Amazon main image have to be on white?</h3>

  <p>Yes, pure white, RGB 255, 255, 255, which is hex #FFFFFF. A background that isn't pure white is a listed suppression reason. Six product types are the exception: beds, bed frames, mattresses, rugs, rug pads and sofas may use a lifestyle main image, with no text or extra logos. Additional images can show the product in use.</p>

  <h3>Why was my Amazon image rejected or suppressed?</h3>

  <p>Amazon lists 14 suppression reasons: text or logos on the main image, a background that isn't pure white, a cropped product, packaging or tags, props, blur, a product too small in the frame and extra items among them. Check the Fix tab in Manage Products and the Content compliance issues report, then upload a compliant replacement with the MAIN code.</p>

  <h3>Can I add text or logos to Amazon product images?</h3>

  <p>Not on the main image: text, logos, graphics and watermarks are a suppression reason. On additional images the guide bans text only on the swatch, but claims such as free shipping, review stars, seller details and Amazon's own logos and badges are banned on every image. Text on a country-specific image must be in that country's language or English.</p>

  <h3>Can I use AI-generated images on Amazon?</h3>

  <p>None of Amazon's image help pages read for this guide bans AI. They ask for a realistic, professional-quality image that shows the real product at its real scale, quantity and color. The one AI rule is about people: photorealistic people generated entirely by AI must be tagged contains-synthetic-performer in the file's XMP dc:subject field before upload.</p>
